{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1494785-dramatic-editing-in-tc-assassins","id":1494785,"title":"Dramatic Editing in TC Assassins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-11T08:26:12-07:00","id":1494785,"title":"Dramatic Editing in TC Assassins","content":"In Assassins there is pointing that a lot of Dramatic Editing comes from players Flashbacks solving now problems. How much coomst each Flashback? They are counted as Inspiration or as Momentum? What are point scales for those? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T04:50:21-07:00","id":1494856,"title":"","content":"That all falls under Dramatic editing in Core, starting on page 154. They're just skinned as flashbacks rather than sudden revelations about the environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T18:02:00-07:00","id":1494894,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s important to point out that the rules for Dramatic Editing don\u2019t care much for how long it was prepared or how improbable it is, but instead on how it impacts the story being told.<br /> <br /> By the original rules DE requires Inspiration, and I personally think it should remain that way, but as you are kind of already limited in the frequency you can DE and most Masteries and many Gifts cost Inspiration to use, so spending Momentum to power DE can be interesting, specially when you have other splats around with far bigger energy pools and recovery of energy than Talents and Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T07:29:03-07:00","id":1494923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1494785-dramatic-editing-in-tc-assassins#post1494785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Assassins there is pointing that a lot of Dramatic Editing comes from players Flashbacks solving now problems. How much coomst each Flashback? They are counted as Inspiration or as Momentum? What are point scales for those? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Assassins pp.100\u2013101: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There are three levels of flashback. Each has an associated Inspiration or Momentum cost, related to the time and effort a character would have needed to expand in the flashback, as well as the advantages the flashback would grant them. <br /> <br /> At the lowest level are 0-point flashbacks \u2026 consider this express permission for a player to claim their character had appropriate gear, retroactively, without feeling the need to push the issue. Optionally, a Storyguide could require a character possess appropriate Skills, Attributes, or Facets before making a 0-point flashback. <br /> <br /> A simple set-up with a single advantage requires spending 1 Inspiration or 2 Momentum. \u2026<br /> <br /> A complicated set-up resulting in either multiple advantages or a single significant one requires spending 2 Inspiration or 4 Momentum. \u2026<br /> <br /> A set-up so intricate, so unlikely, so fortuitous for the characters that it begins to stretch the table's suspension of disbelief, requires spending 3 Inspiration or 6 Momentum, or even more.</div>So it's 0 to 3 Inspiration, or twice that in Momentum. There are also a few alternative costs for flashbacks, such as replacing the costs with per-session usage caps, allowing multiple players to contribute to a flashback, mitigating the cost by incorporating a downside into the flashback, or replacing the Inspiration cost with an appropriate skill roll (similar to how <b>Scion</b>'s Twists of Fate work). <br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm hoping that <b>Assassins</b> is giving us a sneak peek at Dramatic Editing options in the upcoming <b>Talents Player's Guide</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}